**Starting from a working first draft**

{% figure src="projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/inso-app-former-version.jpg" frame="before" alt="The app when I joined: a dense dark list of alerts in capitals, an alert detail packed with text under a small map, and a map that shows a single alert pin." caption="The app demo built by the engineers ==before== I joined the project team." /%}

**A working demo lacking a plan and structure.** When I joined, the engineers had a demo of the app running on TestFlight, built from conversations with {% tip text="country offices" note="INSO has 23 country offices where the team is generally composed of a director, deputy, operations and financial staff, information management staff & field monitoring personnel. (updated 05-2026)" /%}. Scope, requirements and data were still to be defined.

**Designing without direct access to partners.** Partners are the main end users, but I didn't have permission to contact them directly. The country offices offered to act as proxies and supported our research and testing, although it wasn't always straightforward, and the extra layer between us and the users made the process harder and affected the quality of the work. Partners had their say in a survey after launch.
